Q) Spiral Matrix

Explanation:

The task is to return all elements of a matrix in spiral order, starting from the top-left corner and moving clockwise.
To achieve this, we process the matrix layer by layer, shrinking the boundaries after completing each direction.

Key Idea:
  At any point, the unvisited part of the matrix is bounded by four pointers:

  top → first unvisited row
  bottom → last unvisited row
  left → first unvisited column
  right → last unvisited column

  We traverse the matrix in four directions using these boundaries and update them after each traversal.

Approach:

  Initialize four boundaries:
    top = 0, bottom = m - 1
    left = 0, right = n - 1

  Continue looping while:
  top <= bottom AND left <= right  (This ensures we stay within valid bounds.)

  Traverse in the following order:

    a. Left to Right (top row)
        Traverse from left to right on row top
        Increment top after traversal

    b. Top to Bottom (right column)
        Traverse from top to bottom on column right
        Decrement right after traversal
     
    This step is done only if top <= bottom
    c. Right to Left (bottom row)
        Traverse from right to left on row bottom
        Decrement bottom after traversal

    This step is done only if left <= right
    d. Bottom to Top (left column)
        Traverse from bottom to top on column left
        Increment left after traversal

Code:

class Solution {
    public List<Integer> spiralOrder(int[][] matrix) {
        List result = new ArrayList<>();
        int m=matrix.length; int n=matrix[0].length;

        int left=0; int right=n-1;
        int top=0; int bottom = m-1;

        while(top<=bottom && left<=right){
            
            // left to right
            for(int i=left;i<=right;i++){
                result.add(matrix[top][i]);
            }
            top++;

            // top to bottom
            for(int i=top;i<=bottom;i++){
                result.add(matrix[i][right]);
            }
            right--;

            // right to left
            if(top<=bottom){
                for(int i=right;i>=left;i--){
                    result.add(matrix[bottom][i]);
                }
                bottom--;
            }   

            // bottom to top
            if(left<=right){
                for(int i=bottom;i>=top;i--){
                    result.add(matrix[i][left]);    
                }
                left++;
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
}
